From 80c2a9dc054b495a7787f3f5e95d257d7ca76dd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 01:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(Core): Update OnPlayerResurrect override signature for
 bool& hook (I-173)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AC's PlayerScript hook OnPlayerResurrect takes applySickness by
reference (bool&) so scripts can cancel the resurrection sickness
debuff by setting it to false. IPP's override was still declared
with pass-by-value (bool), which fails to override the virtual and
breaks the build under current AC.

IPP doesn't use applySickness (param is commented out), so this is
a pure signature alignment — no behavior change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp b/src/IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp
index 593772f..20f32bd 100644
--- a/src/IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp
+++ b/src/IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ public:
         sIndividualProgression->CheckAdjustments(player);
     }
 
-    void OnPlayerResurrect(Player* player, float /*restore_percent*/, bool /*applySickness*/) override
+    void OnPlayerResurrect(Player* player, float /*restore_percent*/, bool& /*applySickness*/) override
     {
         if (!player || !player->IsInWorld())
             return;
-- 
2.34.1

